{
  "_about": "The places on the sea chart (Robin, 2026-11-20: a sea chart of islands; each island a hunting ground with its own levels; he travels by tapping the chart, no ship to steer). A new hero starts in `start`, and wakes there (at `wake`) after a fall. Only the place he is in is alive: sailing away empties it, arriving fills it from its zones. A zone keeps `count` monsters of one kind inside its box. `chart` is where the place sits on the chart, as shares of its width and height. Sailing is from a dock only (mine: it gives the walk back its weight): he must stand near `dock`, and steps ashore at the other place's `arrive`. A place's layout comes from the Art Director's drop when there is one (tools/place-from-art.mjs writes `land`, `water`, `solids`, `dock`, `arrive`, the chest's spot and the zones' boxes from his place.json): `land` is the shore as a many-cornered outline, outside it is sea; `water` is water inside the land; `solids` are circles to walk round. A place without `land` is its whole box. `biomes` (since 2026-11-20; Robin: 'it should be biomes', then his pick of big islands with several biomes each and the chart between them) are the grounds of a place, each a box with a name and its levels; the screen says the name when he walks into one. A town has none. The three of Crab Cay are Victor, GD's, laid over Leonard, AD's island as it is. Names are Victor, GD's placeholders (docs/names.md).",
